Z||000000||dennis_6||08-31-2001||01:00 PM||||I asked for a motor to fit a 92 Lumina for my engine swap that came with  all accesories,wiring harness, and a computer.<BR>Does either one of these sound like a deal?<P>"hello i have your 3.4 motor here i can get you everything you are asking for to you for @ 1000.00 all of motors are started and tested and have a 120 day warranty thanks<BR>alice."<P>"I can supply you with a 95 Lumina 3.4 complete with wiring and ECM for $1250 plus shipping."<P>Thanks!<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Hank is Here||08-31-2001||01:14 PM||||that engine will not be the easiest swap<BR>the FWD cars have al heads rather than the iron heads of the fiero.  <BR>I would first go for a ohc 3.4 rather than just the normal 3.4 al head.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||08-31-2001||01:18 PM||||Since the 3.4 is primarily the same as the 2.8/3.1, the Fiero heads and intake assembly will bolt directly on- so you'll have some leftover parts from the old engine, and you'll need the donor parts from a Fiero V6.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg"> <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||08-31-2001||01:26 PM||||And the pistons would need to be changed (from what I hear) because the Al head 3.4s use a dished piston that will give a very low compression ratio when used with the Fiero's iron heads.  This is why you don't want to put the Al heads on your Fiero.<P>I may be wrong, but that's what I've read on the Forum.||||reg||4
Z||000004||THE BEAST||08-31-2001||01:47 PM||||Sorry, but I'm not too familiar with which cars came with this engine. So I must ask.<P>Are those 3.4 PR, or the TDC ones?<P>If is the tdc I'll be interested on it!<BR>(Just, if is the TDC, can you get a 96' and a standard trainee from the same engine(3.4 TDC) {I know that the only ones with the standard trainee were the 93'}. But my question is; can you get one?<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000005||87GTZ34||08-31-2001||02:05 PM||||Yes you can couple it to a manual but you can't use the '96 'PCM' as there is no version of code for it that supports a manual transmission.  You can put the earlier 'ECM'and electronics on it but then you will be buying the '96 stuff and throwing it away.  The only 2 advantages to the '96:  a redesigned belt assem that was supposed to make it more reliable but it is only marginal; redesigned head mainly for emissions, it had a faster burn chamber and about a 1/2 point increase in compression.  The result was 10 more horses and 5 more lbsft of torque.  If you get a manual trans you should get the 284 Getrag with gearing to match the 4 valve engine otherwise you may be disappointed with bottom end torque. GL||||reg||1
Z||000006||Standard||08-31-2001||02:06 PM||||The only 3.4's that came in the lumina were the TDC's.  and $1250 for a 3.4 TDC complete is a really really good deal.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">        <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
